      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-17T11:01:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t work with `shared_libs: [\"libbinder_ndk\"]`. The compiler still failed to find binder_ibinder.h.\n\n`include_dirs: [\"frameworks/native/libs/binder/include\"]` also doesn\u0027t work.\n\nWith `include_dirs: [\"frameworks/native/libs/binder/include\"]`:\n```\nmodule \"libvm_payload\" variant \"android_x86_64_silvermont_shared\": module source path \"packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid/vm_payload/frameworks/native/libs/binder/include\" does not exist\n```\nWith `include_dirs: [\"../../../../../frameworks/native/libs/binder/include\"]`:\n```\nmodule \"libvm_payload\" variant \"android_x86_64_silvermont_shared\": Path is outside directory: ../../../../../frameworks/native/libs/binder/include\n```",
      "parentUuid": "b22371b1_66673d68",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b201151386d384d49bbc4d75c81bb99ff5a396ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e76fa6b_3f9e4a3c",
        "filename": "microdroid/vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-13T21:54:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe not for this CL, but do we want vsock and ports to be part of the API? The payload just wants to expose a (RPC) binder interfaces to the host and the implementation details shouldn\u0027t be important.\n\nI\u0027m wondering if we want to head in the direction of:\n\n    AVmPayload_exportServiceToHost(const char *name, AIBinder *service, ...)\n    \nwhere microdroid deals with the details of vsock, allocation of a port and telling VS about the (port, service name) pair so that it can expose it to the host client in the AVF API e.g. `vm.getService(\"MyVmService\")`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 93,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "b201151386d384d49bbc4d75c81bb99ff5a396ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b19320b_4036aae2",
        "filename": "microdroid/vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-13T22:40:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we might want to migrate to that eventually (Inseob had a related bug, which got closed but then reopened I think).\nBut for now I think this simple version is enough - the app controls both sides, so we don\u0027t need a broker for service discovery, and static port numbers work fine.\n\nI was thinking we ought to reserve some ports for Microdroid, but I think the kernel already restricts ports \u003c 1024. (We should check that payloads really can\u0027t use those though.)",
      "parentUuid": "8e76fa6b_3f9e4a3c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 93,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "b201151386d384d49bbc4d75c81bb99ff5a396ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f45a2879_321e86af",
        "filename": "microdroid/vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-14T10:52:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "About this interface:\n```\nAVmPayload_exportServiceToHost(const char *name, AIBinder *service, ...)\n```\nInstead of letting Microdroid handle the port/name mapping, can we use directly the named Unix domain socket internally? Then we don\u0027t need to process this port/name mapping in Microdroid.\n\n+1 later the host can just call `vm.getService(\"MyVmService\")`.",
      "parentUuid": "1b19320b_4036aae2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 93,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "b201151386d384d49bbc4d75c81bb99ff5a396ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
